# Pull the latest code, so deploying is a git push and nothing else.
#
# THIS IS WHAT KEEPS THE PROJECT PHONE-WORKABLE. Without it, every code
# change needs an SSH session; with it, pushing to main is the deploy.
# The recorders cycle hourly, so new code is live within the hour with
# no manual step.
#
# The repo is public, so this needs no credential. `git reset --hard`
# rather than `git pull`, because a merge conflict on an unattended box
# is a recorder that silently stops.
#
# IT UPDATES THE REPO, NOT THE MACHINE. Unit files under
# /etc/systemd/system are copies taken by bootstrap.sh, and nothing here
# rewrites them or reloads systemd — this runs as `marketslap`, which
# has no business writing to /etc. So a change to a .service file in
# deploy/ does NOT deploy: it lands in the repo and is ignored by the
# running box, silently, which is the worst shape a deploy gap can take.
#
# Anything that must take effect without an SSH session therefore
# belongs in CODE, which this does update, rather than in unit config.
# The m15 recorder's source stamp is the worked example: it reads
# systemd's INVOCATION_ID instead of an Environment= line for exactly
# this reason. To change a unit for real, re-run bootstrap.sh — it is
# idempotent and reinstalls the units.

[Unit]
Description=MarketSlap self-update from git
After=network-online.target
Wants=network-online.target

[Service]
Type=oneshot
User=marketslap
WorkingDirectory=/opt/marketslap
ExecStart=/usr/bin/git fetch --quiet origin main
ExecStart=/usr/bin/git reset --hard --quiet origin/main
